  {
   "start": 142.88,
   "end": 164.43,
   "en": "When you sleep, your eyes move quickly — scientists call this dream sleep. Octopuses have something similar! When an octopus falls into deep sleep, its skin starts to flash and change: stripes, spots, waves of color, all dancing across its body. It looks like it is watching a movie behind closed eyes.",
